UPDATE changelog_entries SET content_json = '{"en":{"title":"DSHX 0.2: the DeepSeek Harness 0.2 plugin toolchain, and a migration path for every 0.1 plugin","description":"DSHX 0.2.0-preview.0 is the first release built on DeepSeek Harness 0.2. It removes protocol-1 and rebuilds settings, conversation, RPC, and session handling on the new contracts. Every breaking change has a step in the migration guide.","sections":[{"id":"the-short-version","title":"The short version","paragraphs":["DeepSeek Harness 0.2 changed enough that a compatibility shim would have hidden the work rather than saved it. DSHX 0.2.0-preview.0 is built only on the 0.2 contracts: `protocol-2` replaces `protocol-1`, settings become a plugin `Config`, conversation moves to `uiConversation`, RPC admits peers, and sessions use format 4.","The release is a preview. DSHX and create-dshx are published under npm’s `preview` tag as `0.2.0-preview.0`; `latest` stays on 0.1.3. If you maintain a plugin, start with the [0.1 to 0.2 migration guide](https://dshx.io/en/docs/compatibility#migration). If you are starting a project, `create-dshx` scaffolds the new contracts directly.","The rest of this note explains what changed, what we verified, and what is still missing."]},{"id":"why-break","title":"Why we removed protocol-1","paragraphs":["A dual-generation adapter was possible on paper. In practice it would have meant two settings pipelines, two conversation event services, two RPC admission models, and two session vocabularies in the same package. Every diagnostic would have needed a generation branch, and every bug report a question about which mode the plugin was in.","The bigger problem is that compatibility layers make migrations invisible. A plugin could keep building against 0.1 names while the runtime quietly used 0.2 behavior. That is the kind of drift that surfaces weeks later as a settings form that renders but never persists.","So 0.2 cuts over. `engines.dsh` must declare a range inside `>=0.2.1-rc.2 <0.3.0-0`, and `dshx check` rejects a missing or stale declaration. The [compatibility guide](https://dshx.io/en/docs/compatibility) lists the full status vocabulary."]},{"id":"verified","title":"What we verified, and what the npm artifact is not","paragraphs":["The verified baseline is a source build of the [`dsh-v0.2.1-rc.2` tag](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/releases/tag/dsh-v0.2.1-rc.2). The real-runtime smoke suite starts Host-only and Host/Client projects, writes settings through the revision fence, runs Commands, replays Conversation events, restarts the Host, and exercises runtime Inspect for tools, services, events, and configs.","The npm package published as `@deepseek-ai/dsh@0.2.1-rc.2` is a different artifact. It currently ships stale profile-boot code. We do not mark a version verified because npm resolves it; we mark it verified when the runtime boots and the smoke suite passes. Until upstream republishes, use a source build for development.","That distinction is visible in `dshx check`, in diagnostics, and in the CLI capability output.","| Status | What it means |\n| --- | --- |\n| `verified` | A source build of `dsh-v0.2.1-rc.2` passed the real-runtime smoke suite. |\n| `compatible` | The version is inside the declared range, but no real-runtime evidence exists yet. |\n| `experimental` | A known gap exists, such as the stale npm artifact. |\n| `unsupported` | The version is outside the declared range. |"]},{"id":"settings","title":"Settings: one Config, one entry id, no namespace","paragraphs":["In 0.1, a plugin declared a settings schema and registered it with a Host provider under a namespace it chose. In 0.2, the schema is the plugin Config, and DSH projects it into its own Settings form through `SettingsForms`. There is no namespace field and no registration call.","`defineSettings()` still takes one Schemastery schema, so most schema definitions move unchanged. `defineHost()` now takes a single `config` contract instead of a `settings` array, and `setup` receives the config handle. DSHX marks the root schema volatile so every field is live; marking an individual field volatile now throws.","The identity change is the part that breaks quietly. DSH keys the form by the Host profile entry id that loads the plugin, not by a name the plugin picks. DSHX embeds that id in the Client artifact, so the plugin must keep loading through the entry named in its bundle patch. Rename the entry without updating the patch and the form still renders; it just reads and writes nothing.","On the Client, `useSettings` reads `ctx.configForms.get(entryId)`. `set` and `unset` return booleans, ordered edits use `mutate` with an expected revision, and secret fields report only their schema position and whether a value is set. The value never crosses the wire."]},{"id":"conversation","title":"Conversation: uiConversation and session format 4","paragraphs":["`defineConversation()` keeps its lifecycle shape, but registration moves to `ctx.uiConversation.events.register`. The `conversationEvents` service is gone, renderer types come from `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-conversation/client`, and `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-runtime` is not part of DSH 0.2 at all. Remove it from dependencies, peers, and `dsh.client.inject`.","Session format moves to 4. Only official `SessionEventMap` keys are accepted, sequence values are branded, and custom durable event types remain unsupported. If your plugin persisted session events, there is no translation shim in this release; rebuild the payloads against the official vocabulary.","Replay is the part to test first. The smoke suite replays conversation events on both a fresh Host and a restarted one, because that is where stale sequence assumptions show up."]},{"id":"connection","title":"Connection: peers, remote namespaces, and a launch token","paragraphs":["Host APIs register with `connection.rpc.handle(channel, handler)`. The `authority` option is gone; the handler receives the official `peer` fact and DSH decides admission. Client code no longer calls `connection.api`. Generated Remote namespaces appear as `ctx.remote.<namespace>`, with `$on` and `$stream` for events.","DSHX keeps the author-facing shape of `useApiQuery` and the imperative bindings, and the wire path is unchanged from a plugin’s point of view: top-level `/dshx-<hash>/<method>` channels still carry the method in the DSHX envelope. The capability name changes to `connection:peer-admission`.","One operational change surprises people. Browser requests now require the launch token DSH hands to the page, exchanged at `/connect?token=…` for a signed session cookie before any `/api` call. Direct loopback requests without that cookie fail. Custom smoke runners and scripts need to perform the exchange; the DSHX Client runtime already does."]},{"id":"smaller-breaks","title":"The smaller changes that still break builds","paragraphs":["Most of these are mechanical, and they fail at build or check time rather than at runtime. That makes the migration predictable: fix the compiler first, then fix the behavior."],"items":["Prompt assembly uses `personaPrefix` and `personaSuffix`, and DSH allocates contribution order. The `order` field on `definePromptSection` and `definePromptContext` is now a hint.","Command input exposes `attachments` instead of `images`; `CommandResult` may carry `sourceEventSeq`.","Tools no longer support `mode: both`. Native and PTC tools are declared separately. `ctx.codeRuntime` becomes `ctx.ptcRuntime`, `CallId` becomes `ToolCallId`, and `JsonValue` comes from `@deepseek-ai/dsh-util-values`.","`manifestVersion: 1` is accepted, `engines.dsh` is the preferred support declaration, and `dsh.bundle.patch` may be a string or an array. The `/invariant` subpath is gone.","DSH 0.2 has no runtime Slot catalog. `dshx inspect slots` reports `DSHX3204`, and `dshx add ui` generates from explicit `--slot` and `--provider` values with a `DSHX6112` warning."]},{"id":"migrate","title":"How to migrate a plugin","paragraphs":["The [migration guide](https://dshx.io/en/docs/compatibility#migration) is the reference. The order below matches it and keeps each step verifiable.","A useful first target is the smallest plugin you maintain. Migrate it end to end, run the smoke, and only then move the rest. The failure modes cluster around settings identity and session replay, and one real migration finds them faster than reading the guide twice."],"items":["Update metadata: move `@becomeopc/dshx` to `0.2.0-preview.0`, pin `@deepseek-ai/dsh` to `0.2.1-rc.2` for local builds, add `engines.dsh` with `>=0.2.1-rc.2 <0.3.0-0`, and remove `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-runtime` everywhere.","Move settings: keep the schema, drop the namespace, pass `config` to `defineHost`, read `ctx.configForms` on the Client, and rename capability checks to `client:config-forms`.","Update Conversation: replace `ctx.conversationEvents.register` with `ctx.uiConversation.events.register`, then rebuild against session format 4.","Update Connection: remove the `authority` option, switch Client calls to `ctx.remote` namespaces, and exchange the launch token at `/connect` for browser API access.","Update Prompt, Commands, and Tools: `personaPrefix` and `personaSuffix`, `attachments`, `sourceEventSeq`, `ptcRuntime`, `ToolCallId`, and the official `JsonValue`.","Validate: run `dshx check`, then `pnpm smoke:dsh -- --dsh-source <checkout>`. The source smoke is the only run that exercises the verified path."]},{"id":"not-done","title":"What we did not do","paragraphs":["We did not keep a 0.1 adapter. We did not mark the npm `0.2.1-rc.2` artifact verified. We did not restore the runtime Slot catalog, because DSH 0.2 does not expose one. We did not add a translation layer for custom session events.","We also did not change the author-facing shape of `useApiQuery` or the imperative API bindings. Those keep working as long as the package edges and capability names are updated.","If one of those omissions blocks a real plugin, say so in the issue tracker. The next preview is where they would land."]},{"id":"next","title":"What happens next","paragraphs":["The next preview follows upstream. When `@deepseek-ai/dsh` republishes an artifact that boots, the adapter will record it as verified rather than experimental. Until then, the source tag is the reference.","The 0.2 line also carried forward `create-dshx`, the Phase A fixture, and the reference marketplace plugin. Their tests run in the same `pnpm check:all` gate as the core packages.","For production work, stay on `latest` (0.1.3). For migration work, install `@becomeopc/dshx@preview` and open issues with the exact `dshx check` output."]}],"links":[{"label":"DSHX 0.2.0-preview.0 on npm","href":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@becomeopc/dshx/v/0.2.0-preview.0"},{"label":"create-dshx 0.2.0-preview.0 on npm","href":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/create-dshx/v/0.2.0-preview.0"},{"label":"0.1 to 0.2 migration guide","href":"https://dshx.io/en/docs/compatibility#migration"},{"label":"DeepSeek Harness compatibility and version status","href":"https://dshx.io/en/docs/compatibility"},{"label":"DeepSeek Harness dsh-v0.2.1-rc.2 tag","href":"https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/releases/tag/dsh-v0.2.1-rc.2"},{"label":"DSHX changelog","href":"https://github.com/liyown/dshx/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md"},{"label":"Release commit on GitHub","href":"https://github.com/liyown/dshx/commit/eea4bdb475181f3f777d43672aa4f2b8268ead53"},{"label":"Browse DeepSeek Harness plugins on DSHX","href":"https://dshx.io/en/plugins"}]},"zh":{"title":"DSHX 0.2：DeepSeek Harness 0.2 的插件工具链，以及每个 0.1 插件的迁移路径","description":"DSHX 0.2.0-preview.0 是首个基于 DeepSeek Harness 0.2 构建的版本。它移除 protocol-1，并按新契约重建设置、会话、RPC 与会话数据。每一项破坏性变更都在迁移指南里有对应步骤。","sections":[{"id":"the-short-version","title":"先说结论","paragraphs":["DeepSeek Harness 0.2 的改动大到兼容层会掩盖工作，而不是省下工作。DSHX 0.2.0-preview.0 只建立在 0.2 契约上：`protocol-2` 取代 `protocol-1`，设置变成插件 `Config`，会话迁移到 `uiConversation`，RPC 以 peer 准入，会话数据使用 format 4。","这是一个预览版。DSHX 与 create-dshx 以 `0.2.0-preview.0` 发布在 npm 的 `preview` 标签下，`latest` 仍是 0.1.3。如果你在维护插件，从 [0.1 到 0.2 迁移指南](https://dshx.io/zh/docs/compatibility#migration)开始；如果从零开始，`create-dshx` 会直接生成新契约。","下面说明改了什么、我们验证了什么，以及还有什么没做。"]},{"id":"why-break","title":"为什么移除 protocol-1","paragraphs":["纸面上可以做双代适配器。实际上这意味着同一个包里有两套设置管线、两套会话事件服务、两套 RPC 准入模型和两套会话词汇。每条诊断都要按代分支，每个 bug 报告都要先问插件跑在哪个模式。","更大的问题是兼容层会让迁移变得不可见。插件可以继续按 0.1 的名字构建，运行时却悄悄使用 0.2 的行为。这类漂移往往在几周后以“设置表单能渲染但永远存不进去”的形式出现。","所以 0.2 直接切换。`engines.dsh` 必须声明落在 `>=0.2.1-rc.2 <0.3.0-0` 内的范围，`dshx check` 会拒绝缺失或过期的声明。[兼容性指南](https://dshx.io/zh/docs/compatibility)列出了完整的状态词汇。"]},{"id":"verified","title":"我们验证了什么，npm 产物又是什么","paragraphs":["验证基线是用 [`dsh-v0.2.1-rc.2` 标签](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/releases/tag/dsh-v0.2.1-rc.2)构建的源码。真实运行时 smoke 会启动 Host-only 与 Host/Client 项目、通过 revision 围栏写入设置、运行 Commands、回放 Conversation 事件、重启 Host，并检查 tools、services、events 与 configs 的运行时 Inspect。","npm 上以 `@deepseek-ai/dsh@0.2.1-rc.2` 发布的产物是另一回事。它目前包含过期的 profile 启动代码。我们不会因为 npm 能解析出版本就标记 verified，而是等运行时真的启动、smoke 真的通过才标记。在上游重新发布之前，开发请使用源码构建。","这个区分会出现在 `dshx check`、诊断信息和 CLI 能力输出中。","| 状态 | 含义 |\n| --- | --- |\n| `verified` | `dsh-v0.2.1-rc.2` 的源码构建通过了真实运行时 smoke。 |\n| `compatible` | 版本在声明范围内，但还没有真实运行时证据。 |\n| `experimental` | 存在已知缺口，例如过期的 npm 产物。 |\n| `unsupported` | 版本超出声明范围。 |"]},{"id":"settings","title":"Settings：一份 Config，一个 entry id，没有命名空间","paragraphs":["在 0.1 里，插件声明设置 schema，再以自选命名空间注册到 Host provider。到了 0.2，这份 schema 就是插件 Config，DSH 通过 `SettingsForms` 把它投影成自己的设置表单。没有命名空间字段，也没有注册调用。","`defineSettings()` 仍然接收一份 Schemastery schema，所以大多数定义可以原样迁移。`defineHost()` 改为接收单个 `config` 契约而不是 `settings` 数组，`setup` 会拿到 config 句柄。DSHX 会把根 schema 标记为 volatile，让所有字段实时生效；单独标记某个字段为 volatile 现在会抛错。","真正会静默出问题的是身份。DSH 用加载插件的 Host profile entry id 作为表单标识，而不是插件自选的名字。DSHX 把这个 id 写进 Client 产物，因此插件必须继续通过 bundle patch 中声明的 entry 加载。改了 entry 却没同步 patch，表单仍然会渲染，只是读写都落不到任何地方。","在 Client 端，`useSettings` 读取 `ctx.configForms.get(entryId)`。`set` 与 `unset` 返回布尔值，有序修改使用带 expected revision 的 `mutate`，密钥字段只报告 schema 位置和是否已设置。值本身不会经过网络传输。"]},{"id":"conversation","title":"Conversation：uiConversation 与 session format 4","paragraphs":["`defineConversation()` 的生命周期形状不变，但注册移到 `ctx.uiConversation.events.register`。`conversationEvents` 服务已移除，渲染类型来自 `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-conversation/client`，`@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-runtime` 已不属于 DSH 0.2。请从 dependencies、peers 与 `dsh.client.inject` 中删除它。","会话数据迁移到 format 4。只接受官方 `SessionEventMap` 的键，序列值带有品牌类型，自定义持久事件类型仍不受支持。如果你的插件持久化过会话事件，这次没有翻译层；请按官方词汇重建 payload。","回放要优先测试。smoke 会分别在全新 Host 与重启后的 Host 上回放会话事件，因为过期的序列假设通常在那里暴露。"]},{"id":"connection","title":"连接：peer、remote 命名空间与启动令牌","paragraphs":["Host API 通过 `connection.rpc.handle(channel, handler)` 注册。`authority` 选项已移除，handler 会收到官方 `peer` 事实，由 DSH 决定是否准入。Client 不再调用 `connection.api`，生成的 Remote 命名空间以 `ctx.remote.<namespace>` 出现，事件使用 `$on` 与 `$stream`。","DSHX 保留了 `useApiQuery` 与命令式绑定的作者接口，插件视角下的线上路径也没有变化：顶层 `/dshx-<hash>/<method>` 通道仍在 DSHX envelope 中携带方法名。能力名称改为 `connection:peer-admission`。","有一处运营层面的变化容易让人措手不及。浏览器请求现在需要 DSH 交给页面的启动令牌，先访问 `/connect?token=…` 换取签名会话 cookie，之后才能调用 `/api`。没有该 cookie 的本地直连请求会失败。自定义 smoke runner 与脚本需要完成这次兑换，DSHX 自己的 Client 运行时已经内置。"]},{"id":"smaller-breaks","title":"那些同样会打断构建的小改动","paragraphs":["大多数是机械改动，而且会在构建或检查阶段失败，而不是运行时。迁移因此是可预测的：先让编译器通过，再修行为。"],"items":["Prompt 组装使用 `personaPrefix` 与 `personaSuffix`，贡献顺序由 DSH 统一分配。`definePromptSection` 与 `definePromptContext` 的 `order` 现在只是提示。","Command 输入使用 `attachments` 取代 `images`；`CommandResult` 可以携带 `sourceEventSeq`。","Tool 不再支持 `mode: both`，native 与 PTC 工具分别声明。`ctx.codeRuntime` 改为 `ctx.ptcRuntime`，`CallId` 改为 `ToolCallId`，`JsonValue` 来自 `@deepseek-ai/dsh-util-values`。","接受 `manifestVersion: 1`，`engines.dsh` 是首选的支持声明，`dsh.bundle.patch` 可以是字符串或数组。`/invariant` 子路径已移除。","DSH 0.2 没有运行时 Slot 目录。`dshx inspect slots` 返回 `DSHX3204`，`dshx add ui` 根据显式的 `--slot` 与 `--provider` 生成，并给出 `DSHX6112` 警告。"]},{"id":"migrate","title":"如何迁移插件","paragraphs":["[迁移指南](https://dshx.io/zh/docs/compatibility#migration)是完整参考。下面的顺序与它一致，每一步都能单独验证。","先拿你维护的最小插件做目标。完整迁移一个、跑通 smoke，再把其余插件跟上。失败模式集中在设置身份与会话回放，一次真实迁移比读两遍指南更容易找到它们。"],"items":["更新元数据：把 `@becomeopc/dshx` 升到 `0.2.0-preview.0`，本地构建固定 `@deepseek-ai/dsh` 为 `0.2.1-rc.2`，加入 `engines.dsh`（`>=0.2.1-rc.2 <0.3.0-0`），并彻底移除 `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-runtime`。","迁移设置：保留 schema，去掉命名空间，把 `config` 传给 `defineHost`，在 Client 读取 `ctx.configForms`，并把能力检查改为 `client:config-forms`。","迁移 Conversation：用 `ctx.uiConversation.events.register` 替换 `ctx.conversationEvents.register`，再按 session format 4 重建。","迁移连接：移除 `authority` 选项，Client 改用 `ctx.remote` 命名空间，浏览器 API 先在 `/connect` 兑换启动令牌。","迁移 Prompt、Commands 与 Tools：`personaPrefix` 与 `personaSuffix`、`attachments`、`sourceEventSeq`、`ptcRuntime`、`ToolCallId` 以及官方 `JsonValue`。","验证：先跑 `dshx check`，再跑 `pnpm smoke:dsh -- --dsh-source <checkout>`。只有源码 smoke 走的是已验证路径。"]},{"id":"not-done","title":"我们没有做什么","paragraphs":["我们没有保留 0.1 适配器。没有把 npm 上的 `0.2.1-rc.2` 产物标记为已验证。没有恢复运行时 Slot 目录，因为 DSH 0.2 不提供。也没有为自定义会话事件增加翻译层。","我们同样没有改变 `useApiQuery` 或命令式 API 绑定的作者接口。只要包边界和能力名称更新，它们会继续工作。","如果这些省略挡住了真实插件，请在 issue tracker 里说明。下一个预览版就是它们可能落地的地方。"]},{"id":"next","title":"接下来会发生什么","paragraphs":["下一个预览版跟随上游。当 `@deepseek-ai/dsh` 重新发布一个能启动的产物，适配器会把它记录为 verified，而不是 experimental。在那之前，源码标签就是参考。","0.2 线也带上了 `create-dshx`、Phase A fixture 与参考 marketplace 插件。它们的测试与核心包一起跑在 `pnpm check:all` 里。","生产环境请留在 `latest`（0.1.3）。做迁移时安装 `@becomeopc/dshx@preview`，并在 issue 里附上完整的 `dshx check` 输出。"]}],"links":[{"label":"npm 上的 DSHX 0.2.0-preview.0","href":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@becomeopc/dshx/v/0.2.0-preview.0"},{"label":"npm 上的 create-dshx 0.2.0-preview.0","href":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/create-dshx/v/0.2.0-preview.0"},{"label":"0.1 到 0.2 迁移指南","href":"https://dshx.io/zh/docs/compatibility#migration"},{"label":"DeepSeek Harness 兼容性与版本状态","href":"https://dshx.io/zh/docs/compatibility"},{"label":"DeepSeek Harness dsh-v0.2.1-rc.2 标签","href":"https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/releases/tag/dsh-v0.2.1-rc.2"},{"label":"DSHX 更新日志","href":"https://github.com/liyown/dshx/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md"},{"label":"GitHub 发布提交","href":"https://github.com/liyown/dshx/commit/eea4bdb475181f3f777d43672aa4f2b8268ead53"},{"label":"浏览 DSHX 上的 DeepSeek Harness 插件","href":"https://dshx.io/zh/plugins"}]}}', revision = revision + 1, updated_at = strftime('%s','now') * 1000 WHERE slug = 'dshx-0-2-0-preview-0';
--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE changelog_entries SET content_json = '{"en":{"title":"Hub CLI 0.1.3: the operations prompt is fetched, not shipped","description":"Hub CLI 0.1.3-preview.0 removes the operations prompt from the public npm package. Every run now fetches an administrator-only bundle with the current instructions, a pinned CLI version, and encrypted resources. The old ops prompt command is gone.","sections":[{"id":"cadence","title":"The prompt was shipping on the wrong cadence","paragraphs":["The [operations prompt](https://dshx.io/en/docs/prompt) is the most frequently edited file in the project. It defines how the agent researches, what it may write, how it reports, and what it must never expose. Those rules change as the catalog grows. The CLI does not.","For a while, every prompt edit meant a new npm release, and an operator could keep running an old prompt long after an administrator changed the rules. The public tarball also carried administrator-facing instructions and resource-handling details that have nothing to do with the command surface.","0.1.3 separates the two. The npm package keeps the commands. The Hub keeps the instructions."]},{"id":"run","title":"What a run looks like now","paragraphs":["An administrator starts a session with a short bootstrap. It points the agent at `dshx-hub ops bundle --output <absolute private path>` through the pinned CLI on npm’s `preview` channel.","The command returns one file. The agent reads `bundle.prompt`, sets each `bundle.resources` key as an environment variable, and uses `bundle.meta.cliVersion` for every later command. It never prints the resource values.","From there the run is the one operators already know: `ops preflight`, `ops begin`, per-write run IDs, checkpoints, a published report, `report latest`, and `ops finish`."]},{"id":"bundle","title":"What the bundle contains","paragraphs":["The file is written with mode `0600`. The CLI never echoes it to the terminal, which keeps resource values out of shell history and logs.","| Field | Contents |\n| --- | --- |\n| `bootstrap` | The short text an administrator pastes into a new agent session. |\n| `prompt` | The full operating instructions: start checklist, editorial policy, error handling, reporting rules. |\n| `meta` | The CLI version, capabilities hash, command surface, and policy values the prompt refers to. |\n| `resources` | Administrator-configured values, decrypted only for this authenticated response. |"]},{"id":"drift","title":"Version drift stops a run instead of degrading it","paragraphs":["The bootstrap stays on the stable `preview` channel, so it does not need to be re-copied when the CLI moves. If the installed CLI and the bundle disagree, the command returns `agent_bundle_mismatch` with `error.details.expectedCliVersion`.","The agent re-runs the same command with that exact version, at most twice. If it still fails, the run stops with the original error. There is no fallback to a remembered prompt: if the bundle is unavailable, the agent cannot know whether its instructions are current.","This is deliberate. A stale prompt is a correctness problem, not a convenience problem."]},{"id":"secrets","title":"What the Hub stores, and what the CLI sees","paragraphs":["Resource values are encrypted with AES-GCM before they reach D1, using the `AGENT_RESOURCE_KEY` Worker secret. They are decrypted only for an authenticated administrator bundle. Rotating the key means re-saving the stored values.","The prompt still forbids tokens, email addresses, private URLs, local paths, raw stack traces, and internal audit payloads in reports. Reports are publishable as-is; anything that would need redaction is disallowed at write time.","The operations state directory stays private and persistent. Checkpoints and locks are local; the Hub only learns a run ID when a report is published."]},{"id":"operator","title":"What changes for operators","items":["`ops prompt` is gone. Any workflow that called it should fetch `ops bundle` instead.","`ops preflight` and `ops begin` are unchanged. Keep `runId`, `stopStartingAt`, and `leaseExpiresAt` from the response.","Writes still carry the run ID, checkpoints still record confirmed stages, and `ops finish` still requires a verified report."]},{"id":"same","title":"What stays the same","paragraphs":["The catalog operations are untouched: source inspection, observation upserts, revisioned curation, visibility, submissions, media, audit, blog, featured shelves, and immutable reports.","So are the response envelope, partial-failure exit codes, idempotency rules, and report immutability. HTTP 200 can still contain rejected batch items, and exit code 2 still means partial success."]},{"id":"tested","title":"How the boundary is tested","paragraphs":["CI checks the Hub snapshot for drift, and release verification rejects any public CLI tarball that contains prompt files. That second check is the important one: it makes the separation a release gate instead of a convention.","The CLI tests cover authentication, scope errors, bundle mismatch, and the resource redaction path. The operations smoke runs against a local Hub and a real D1."]},{"id":"judge","title":"How to judge whether it works","paragraphs":["The output is public. Read a few days of the [daily operations reports](https://dshx.io/en/operations). If the agent cites sources, separates research from confirmed writes, and states open items plainly, the flow is working.","If reports turn vague, start with the prompt rather than the CLI. The prompt is now editable without a release, which is the point of this change."]},{"id":"availability","title":"Availability","paragraphs":["Hub CLI 0.1.3-preview.0 is on npm’s preview channel; `latest` remains 0.1.1. The [package changelog](https://github.com/liyown/dshx/blob/main/packages/framework-hub-cli/CHANGELOG.md) has the full diff.","Administrators should review the prompt page and confirm the resource allowlist before the next scheduled run."]}],"links":[{"label":"Hub CLI 0.1.3-preview.0 on npm","href":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@becomeopc/dshx-hub-cli/v/0.1.3-preview.0"},{"label":"Hub CLI release notes","href":"https://github.com/liyown/dshx/blob/main/packages/framework-hub-cli/CHANGELOG.md"},{"label":"Read the public daily operations reports","href":"https://dshx.io/en/operations"},{"label":"DSHX Hub changelog","href":"https://dshx.io/en/changelog"}]},"zh":{"title":"Hub CLI 0.1.3：运营提示词改为按需获取","description":"Hub CLI 0.1.3-preview.0 把运营提示词从公开 npm 包中移除。每轮运营改为获取管理员专属 bundle，其中包含当前说明、锁定的 CLI 版本与加密资源。旧的 ops prompt 命令已移除。","sections":[{"id":"cadence","title":"提示词和 CLI 的发布节奏本来就不一样","paragraphs":["[运营提示词](https://dshx.io/zh/docs/prompt)是这个项目里被修改最频繁的文件。它规定 Agent 如何调研、可以写什么、如何汇报，以及绝不能暴露什么。这些规则随目录成长而调整，CLI 不会。","有一段时间，每改一次提示词就要发一个新的 npm 版本，而管理员改了规则之后，运营端可能仍在跑旧提示词。公开 tarball 里还带着面向管理员的说明和资源处理细节，它们与命令面无关。","0.1.3 把两者分开。npm 包保留命令，Hub 保留说明。"]},{"id":"run","title":"现在一轮运营怎么跑","paragraphs":["管理员用一段很短的引导语开始会话。它让 Agent 通过 npm `preview` 通道上固定的 CLI 运行 `dshx-hub ops bundle --output <绝对且私密的路径>`。","命令返回一个文件。Agent 读取 `bundle.prompt`，把 `bundle.resources` 中的每个键设置为本轮环境变量，并在之后所有命令中使用 `bundle.meta.cliVersion`。资源值从不打印。","之后就是运营熟悉的流程：`ops preflight`、`ops begin`、每次写入携带 run ID、checkpoint、发布报告、`report latest`、`ops finish`。"]},{"id":"bundle","title":"bundle 里有什么","paragraphs":["文件以 `0600` 权限写入。CLI 不会把内容回显到终端，资源值因此不会进入 shell 历史与日志。","| 字段 | 内容 |\n| --- | --- |\n| `bootstrap` | 管理员粘贴到新 Agent 会话里的短引导语。 |\n| `prompt` | 完整操作说明：启动清单、编辑政策、错误处理、报告规则。 |\n| `meta` | CLI 版本、能力哈希、命令面，以及提示词引用的策略参数。 |\n| `resources` | 管理员配置的值，只在这份通过认证的响应中解密。 |"]},{"id":"drift","title":"版本不一致会中止运行，而不是降级","paragraphs":["引导语固定在稳定的 `preview` 通道上，CLI 前进时不需要重新复制。如果本地 CLI 与 bundle 不一致，命令会返回 `agent_bundle_mismatch`，并给出 `error.details.expectedCliVersion`。","Agent 会用这个确切版本重跑同一条命令，最多两次。仍然失败就以原始错误停止。没有“记住的旧提示词”可用：bundle 不可用时，Agent 无法确认自己的说明是否最新。","这是有意设计的。过期提示词是正确性问题，不是便利性问题。"]},{"id":"secrets","title":"Hub 存什么，CLI 看到什么","paragraphs":["资源值在写入 D1 之前用 AES-GCM 加密，密钥是 `AGENT_RESOURCE_KEY` Worker secret。只有通过认证的管理员 bundle 才会解密。轮换密钥意味着重新保存这些值。","提示词仍然禁止在报告中出现 token、邮箱地址、私有 URL、本地路径、原始堆栈与内部审计 payload。报告要能原样发布，任何需要在发布前打码的内容，在写入时就不允许出现。","运营状态目录保持私有且持久。checkpoint 与锁都在本地，Hub 只有在报告发布时才得知 run ID。"]},{"id":"operator","title":"运营侧的变化","items":["`ops prompt` 已移除。任何调用它的流程都应改为获取 `ops bundle`。","`ops preflight` 与 `ops begin` 不变。保存响应中的 `runId`、`stopStartingAt` 与 `leaseExpiresAt`。","写入仍携带 run ID，checkpoint 仍记录已确认阶段，`ops finish` 仍要求报告已验证。"]},{"id":"same","title":"哪些部分不变","paragraphs":["目录操作没有变化：来源检查、observation upsert、带 revision 的内容编辑、可见性、投稿、媒体、审计、博客、精选榜单，以及不可变的运营报告。","响应 envelope、部分失败退出码、幂等规则与报告不可变性也没有变化。HTTP 200 仍可能包含被拒绝的批次条目，退出码 2 仍然表示部分成功。"]},{"id":"tested","title":"这条边界如何被测试","paragraphs":["CI 会检查 Hub 快照是否漂移，发布验证会拒绝任何包含提示词文件的公开 CLI tarball。第二个检查更重要：它让分离成为发布门槛，而不是约定。","CLI 测试覆盖认证、权限错误、bundle 不匹配与资源脱敏路径。运营 smoke 则跑在本地 Hub 与真实 D1 上。"]},{"id":"judge","title":"如何判断它是否在工作","paragraphs":["产出是公开的。读几天[每日运营报告](https://dshx.io/zh/operations)。如果 Agent 引用来源、区分调研与已确认写入、并直接列出未完成事项，说明流程正常。","如果报告开始变得含糊，先检查提示词，而不是 CLI。提示词现在不发布版本也能修改，这正是本次改动的意义。"]},{"id":"availability","title":"获取方式","paragraphs":["Hub CLI 0.1.3-preview.0 在 npm 的 preview 通道上，`latest` 仍为 0.1.1。完整差异见[包的 changelog](https://github.com/liyown/dshx/blob/main/packages/framework-hub-cli/CHANGELOG.md)。","管理员应在下一次计划运行前审阅提示词页面，并确认资源白名单。"]}],"links":[{"label":"npm 上的 Hub CLI 0.1.3-preview.0","href":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@becomeopc/dshx-hub-cli/v/0.1.3-preview.0"},{"label":"Hub CLI 发布记录","href":"https://github.com/liyown/dshx/blob/main/packages/framework-hub-cli/CHANGELOG.md"},{"label":"阅读公开的每日运营报告","href":"https://dshx.io/zh/operations"},{"label":"DSHX Hub 更新日志","href":"https://dshx.io/zh/changelog"}]}}', revision = revision + 1, updated_at = strftime('%s','now') * 1000 WHERE slug = 'hub-cli-0-1-3-preview-0';
--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE changelog_entries SET content_json = '{"en":{"title":"Why DSHX Hub now has a plugin journal and ten curated shelves","description":"DSHX Hub published a bilingual journal and ten shelves covering 52 DeepSeek Harness plugins. Here is how the picks were made, what featured does not mean, and how the shelves stay current.","sections":[{"id":"why","title":"Fifty-two plugins is past the point where a list is enough","paragraphs":["A catalog can tell you that 52 DeepSeek Harness plugins exist. It cannot tell you which three are worth an afternoon. Search answers existence; stars measure attention; a flat category list puts a skin, a memory layer, and a remote-control bridge in the same row.","The [featured page](https://dshx.io/en/featured) is the missing layer: 52 plugins arranged into ten shelves by the job they do, in an order an editor is willing to defend.","It is not a ranking. There is no score, no vote count, and no paid placement."]},{"id":"shelves","title":"The ten shelves","paragraphs":["Skins and Interface, Remote and Mobile, Memory and Context, Models and Access, Agents and Automation, Developer Workbench, Browser and Multimodal, Markets and Trust, Session and Rewind, and Fun and Experiments.","Each shelf is ordered. Empty shelves are cleared rather than kept with stale picks. Every pick links to its [plugin page](https://dshx.io/en/plugins), so a reader can go from a recommendation to the install target in one step."]},{"id":"meaning","title":"What a pick means, and what it does not","paragraphs":["A pick means an editor read the source, the README, and the install target, and judged the plugin worth trying for that job. It is not a security review, a compatibility guarantee, or a promise that the plugin survives the next DSH release.","Featured is separate from the quality flag the catalog computes, and separate from search ranking. A plugin can be excellent and absent because the shelf is full or the job is already covered.","The first journal article makes that boundary explicit: [Curating 52 DeepSeek Harness Plugins](https://dshx.io/en/blog/curating-52-deepseek-harness-plugins)."]},{"id":"journal","title":"The journal","paragraphs":["Articles are longer than a changelog entry and shorter than documentation. They explain how a plugin was evaluated, how a category is changing, or how to get a tool running when the README assumes too much.","The launch pieces are the curation article and a full install guide for [dsh-whale-widget](https://dshx.io/en/blog/dsh-whale-widget-guide), a free DSH Web balance widget. The guide covers install commands, bubble setup, and the fixes people actually need.","Future posts follow the same rule: one subject, evidence you can check, and a clear statement of what the article leaves out."]},{"id":"choosing","title":"How a plugin gets picked, and removed","paragraphs":["Picks come from source evidence: README, repository activity, declared install target, publisher facts, and the public Hub entry. Only published plugins appear; hidden entries drop out even if they were picked earlier.","Shelves are re-checked when a plugin changes version, when a repository goes quiet, or when a better option appears for the same job. Removal is not a verdict on the author. Usually the plugin moved, the target changed, or the category found a better answer.","Article links follow the same rule: a link to a plugin that is later hidden gets corrected."]},{"id":"limits","title":"What this first version gets wrong","paragraphs":["Ten shelves force choices. Some plugins fit two shelves and appear once; some categories are thin because the ecosystem is still small. The list is a snapshot of October 2026, not a permanent taxonomy.","The bilingual copy is checked for factual parity, not literary equivalence. If a Chinese description reads flatter than the English one, that is a bug worth reporting.","The shelves do not cover every plugin, and they are not meant to. Search and category pages remain the complete index."]},{"id":"authors","title":"For plugin authors","items":["Publish a stable identity and one unambiguous, structurally safe install target.","Write a README that covers what the plugin does, how to configure it, and its limitations. The Hub keeps the original README and records its content hash.","Provide bilingual names, short descriptions, and overviews that stand on their own. Placeholder copy and generic keyword lists are rejected.","Choose accurate categories and tags. A plugin that is honest about its scope is easier to place on a shelf.","Keep the entry current. A stale version, a dead repository, or a broken install target is a reason to remove a pick."]},{"id":"next","title":"What is next","paragraphs":["More install guides for plugins with non-obvious setup, category reviews that compare several options for the same job, and migration notes when a DSH release changes a contract.","Articles are published only when there is evidence. A post that repeats a README adds little; one that explains a trade-off or a failure mode is worth the page.","Follow the [journal](https://dshx.io/en/blog) or the [changelog](https://dshx.io/en/changelog)."]}],"links":[{"label":"Read the DSHX Hub journal","href":"https://dshx.io/en/blog"},{"label":"Browse featured DeepSeek Harness plugins","href":"https://dshx.io/en/featured"},{"label":"Curating 52 DeepSeek Harness plugins","href":"https://dshx.io/en/blog/curating-52-deepseek-harness-plugins"},{"label":"dsh-whale-widget: DSH balance widget install guide","href":"https://dshx.io/en/blog/dsh-whale-widget-guide"},{"label":"Browse all DeepSeek Harness plugins","href":"https://dshx.io/en/plugins"},{"label":"DSHX Hub changelog","href":"https://dshx.io/en/changelog"}]},"zh":{"title":"DSHX Hub 为什么新增插件博客与十个精选榜单","description":"DSHX Hub 上线了双语博客，以及覆盖 52 个 DeepSeek Harness 插件的十个榜单。这里说明推荐如何选出、featured 不代表什么，以及榜单如何保持更新。","sections":[{"id":"why","title":"52 个插件，已经不能只靠列表","paragraphs":["目录可以告诉你存在 52 个 DeepSeek Harness 插件，却无法告诉你哪三个值得花一个下午。搜索回答存在性，star 数衡量关注度，扁平分类列表会把皮肤、记忆层和远程控制桥接放进同一行。","[精选页](https://dshx.io/zh/featured)补的就是这一层：按任务把 52 个插件整理成十个榜单，并给出编辑愿意为之负责的顺序。","它不是排行榜。没有评分，没有票数，也没有付费位置。"]},{"id":"shelves","title":"十个榜单","paragraphs":["它们分别是皮肤与界面、远程与移动、记忆与上下文、模型与接入、Agent 与自动化、开发者工作台、浏览器与多模态、市场与信任、会话与回溯、趣味与实验。","每个榜单都是有序的。没有有效推荐的榜单会被清空，而不是保留过期条目。每个推荐都链接到[插件页面](https://dshx.io/zh/plugins)，读者可以从推荐一步走到安装目标。"]},{"id":"meaning","title":"推荐意味着什么，不意味着什么","paragraphs":["推荐意味着编辑看过源码、README 与安装目标，并判断这个插件值得为该任务一试。它不是安全审查，不是兼容性保证，也不承诺插件在下一个 DSH 版本之后仍然可用。","精选与目录计算的质量标记是两回事，也与搜索排序无关。一个插件可能很优秀却不在榜单上，因为榜单满了，或这个任务已有更合适的答案。","首批文章把这条边界写清楚了：[52 个 DeepSeek Harness 插件的整理记录](https://dshx.io/zh/blog/curating-52-deepseek-harness-plugins)。"]},{"id":"journal","title":"博客","paragraphs":["文章比更新日志长，比文档短。它们解释一个插件如何被评估、某个分类正在发生什么变化，或者当 README 假设太多时，如何把工具真正跑起来。","首批文章是榜单整理记录，以及 [dsh-whale-widget](https://dshx.io/zh/blog/dsh-whale-widget-guide) 的完整安装指南。后者是一个免费的 DSH Web 余额挂件，指南覆盖安装命令、气泡设置，以及用户实际会遇到的修复方法。","之后的文章遵循同一规则：一个主题，可核对的证据，并明确说明文章没有覆盖什么。"]},{"id":"choosing","title":"推荐如何选出，又如何退役","paragraphs":["推荐来自来源证据：README、仓库活跃度、声明的安装目标、发布者信息，以及插件在 Hub 上的公开条目。只有已发布插件会出现；被隐藏的条目即使曾经入选也会退出。","插件版本变化、仓库长期没有动静，或同一任务出现更好的选择时，榜单会重新检查。移除推荐并不代表对作者的评价，通常只是插件迁移了、安装目标变了，或这个分类有了更好的答案。","文章链接遵循同一规则：如果指向的插件后来被隐藏，链接会被修正。"]},{"id":"limits","title":"第一版哪里还不好","paragraphs":["十个榜单意味着取舍。有些插件同时适合两个榜单，却只出现一次；有些分类内容偏薄，因为生态本身还小。这份列表是 2026 年 10 月的快照，不是永久分类法。","双语内容会检查事实一致，而不是文学对等。如果中文描述读起来比英文更平淡，那是一个值得报告的缺陷。","榜单不覆盖所有插件，也不打算覆盖。搜索与分类页面仍然是完整索引。"]},{"id":"authors","title":"插件作者如何进入候选","items":["提供稳定的身份，以及一个明确、结构安全的安装目标。","README 要说明插件做什么、如何配置，以及有哪些限制。Hub 保留原始 README，并记录其内容哈希。","提供能独立成立的双语名称、简短描述与概览。占位文案和泛化关键词列表会被拒绝。","选择准确的分类与标签。对自己的适用范围诚实的插件，更容易被放进合适的榜单。","保持条目更新。版本过期、仓库失效或安装目标损坏，都是移除推荐的理由。"]},{"id":"next","title":"接下来写什么","paragraphs":["更多安装步骤不直观的插件指南、同一任务的多个方案对比，以及 DSH 版本变更契约时的迁移说明。","只有证据充分的文章才会发布。重复 README 的文章价值有限；讲清取舍或失败模式的文章才值得单独成篇。","可以关注[博客](https://dshx.io/zh/blog)或[更新日志](https://dshx.io/zh/changelog)。"]}],"links":[{"label":"阅读 DSHX Hub 博客","href":"https://dshx.io/zh/blog"},{"label":"浏览精选 DeepSeek Harness 插件","href":"https://dshx.io/zh/featured"},{"label":"52 个 DeepSeek Harness 插件的整理记录","href":"https://dshx.io/zh/blog/curating-52-deepseek-harness-plugins"},{"label":"dsh-whale-widget 余额挂件安装指南","href":"https://dshx.io/zh/blog/dsh-whale-widget-guide"},{"label":"浏览全部 DeepSeek Harness 插件","href":"https://dshx.io/zh/plugins"},{"label":"DSHX Hub 更新日志","href":"https://dshx.io/zh/changelog"}]}}', revision = revision + 1, updated_at = strftime('%s','now') * 1000 WHERE slug = 'hub-editorial-blog-and-featured-shelves';
--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE changelog_entries SET content_json = '{"en":{"title":"DSHX Hub now publishes a daily operations log","description":"Every day the catalog is maintained, DSHX Hub publishes what the agent researched, what it changed, and what is still open. Reports are immutable Markdown, merged into one page per Asia/Shanghai day.","sections":[{"id":"receipts","title":"A catalog that edits itself needs receipts","paragraphs":["DSHX Hub is maintained by an autonomous operations agent. It searches the ecosystem, inspects sources, admits plugins, edits copy, and fixes metadata. Some days it changes a lot; some days it decides nothing is worth changing.","The [daily operations log](https://dshx.io/en/operations) records which happened. Each report says what the agent looked at, what it changed, what it could not verify, and what it deliberately skipped.","Without that record, readers can only see the result and guess at the reasoning. The log makes the reasoning part of the product."]},{"id":"day","title":"One page per day","paragraphs":["The agent can run several times a day. Each run used to publish its own report, which turned the history into short notes that were hard to follow.","Reports now group by the Asia/Shanghai calendar day. The newest report is the page body. When it is cumulative and starts with the daily merge marker, earlier runs are hidden; without the marker, they stay in a collapsed section so pre-merge work is not lost.","The page shows the run count, first start, latest completion, and combined outcome. Up to 20 earlier runs are listed, with a count of any beyond that. The [2026-10-21 report](https://dshx.io/en/operations/2026-10-21) is a normal example."]},{"id":"anatomy","title":"Anatomy of a report","items":["Summary: what the run set out to do and what changed.","Work completed: confirmed writes, with the plugin and the action.","Evidence and verification: sources checked and the results that supported a claim.","Open items: material work left incomplete, blockers, and what would resolve them."],"paragraphs":["The headings are stable so same-day reports merge cleanly, and so a reader can compare two days without re-learning the layout."]},{"id":"labels","title":"How to read the labels","paragraphs":["The most useful distinction is between research, attempted writes, confirmed writes, and skipped work. A candidate was not necessarily admitted; an attempted write was not necessarily confirmed.","A zero-write day can be honest. The [operations prompt](https://dshx.io/en/docs/prompt) requires a minimum research effort before declaring that nothing was worth changing, and it requires the queries and rejection reasons to be recorded. A claim without a receipt is a bug.","Reports end as `completed` or `partial`. `partial` means material work was left unfinished; it is more useful than rounding up."]},{"id":"markdown","title":"Why Markdown, and what the renderer allows","paragraphs":["Markdown is the format the agent already writes. It handles tables and lists, and it diffs cleanly when the prompt or template changes.","The Hub renders reports through a restricted pipeline: no raw HTML, no images, no tracking pixels. The daily merge marker is an HTML comment, so it is stripped from the visible page.","Both locales follow the same rules. English and Chinese carry the same facts and conclusions, not a thin translation of each other."]},{"id":"related","title":"The plugin list is a window, not a changelog","paragraphs":["Each page lists the plugins the run touched, with actions from the audit ledger. The association uses the report actor and a server-clock window based on the 60-minute run lease, because the CLI keeps checkpoints locally and the Hub learns the run ID only when the report is published.","A plugin can change outside that window. The report body remains the authoritative account; the list is a navigation aid."]},{"id":"omitted","title":"What we leave out","items":["Credentials, token prefixes, and authentication headers.","Email addresses, private URLs, and local file paths.","Raw stack traces and internal audit payloads.","Raw HTML, images, and tracking pixels."],"paragraphs":["These exclusions are part of the reporting contract, not an afterthought. A report is meant to be publishable as-is, so anything that would need redaction before publication is disallowed at write time."]},{"id":"why","title":"Why publish the process","paragraphs":["Most catalogs publish outcomes and keep the process private. The opposite costs something: mistakes are visible, and so are slow days.","What it buys is a catalog that can be audited. If a description looks wrong, the report shows which source was read. If a plugin disappears, the report says why. That is a firmer basis for trust than a badge.","It also makes the agent easier to improve. A vague report or a skipped verification is a visible failure, and the next prompt revision can target it."]},{"id":"follow","title":"Where to follow","paragraphs":["The log lives at `/operations` and is grouped by day. Day URLs are stable; older run-based URLs redirect with a 301.","The [changelog](https://dshx.io/en/changelog) covers product changes. The [journal](https://dshx.io/en/blog) covers the plugin ecosystem."]}],"links":[{"label":"Read the daily operations reports","href":"https://dshx.io/en/operations"},{"label":"Operations report for 2026-10-21","href":"https://dshx.io/en/operations/2026-10-21"},{"label":"DSHX Hub changelog","href":"https://dshx.io/en/changelog"},{"label":"Read the DSHX Hub journal","href":"https://dshx.io/en/blog"},{"label":"Browse DeepSeek Harness plugins","href":"https://dshx.io/en/plugins"}]},"zh":{"title":"DSHX Hub 开始发布每日运营日志","description":"目录维护的每一天，DSHX Hub 都会发布运营日志：Agent 研究过什么、改了什么、什么仍未完成。报告是不可变的 Markdown，按 Asia/Shanghai 的一天合并成一个页面。","sections":[{"id":"receipts","title":"会自己编辑的目录需要凭证","paragraphs":["DSHX Hub 由自动化运营 Agent 维护。它会搜索生态、检查来源、收录插件、修改文案、修复元数据。有些日子改动很多，有些日子它判断没有值得改的内容。","[每日运营日志](https://dshx.io/zh/operations)记录的是哪一种。每份报告说明 Agent 看过什么、改了什么、哪些无法验证，以及哪些工作被有意跳过。","没有这份记录，读者只能看到结果，再去猜原因。日志让推理过程也成为产品的一部分。"]},{"id":"day","title":"一天一个页面","paragraphs":["Agent 一天可能运行多次。过去每次运行都单独发布报告，历史被切成一堆难读的短记录。","现在报告按 Asia/Shanghai 日历日归组。当天最新的一份作为页面正文；如果它是累计报告并以每日合并标记开头，较早的运行会被隐藏；没有标记时，它们保留在折叠区域，因此合并规则生效之前的工作不会丢失。","页面显示当天的运行次数、最早开始时间、最新完成时间与合并结果。最多列出 20 次较早运行，并说明还有多少未展示。[2026-10-21 的报告](https://dshx.io/zh/operations/2026-10-21)是一个普通例子。"]},{"id":"anatomy","title":"一份报告的结构","items":["Summary：这一轮打算做什么，实际改了什么。","Work completed：已确认的写入，以及对应的插件与操作。","Evidence and verification：检查过的来源，以及支持结论的结果。","Open items：未完成的重要工作、阻塞项，以及解决它们需要什么。"],"paragraphs":["标题保持稳定，同一天的报告才能干净地合并，读者比较两天时也不需要重新适应版式。"]},{"id":"labels","title":"如何读懂报告里的标签","paragraphs":["最有用的区分是调研、尝试写入、确认写入与跳过的工作。候选并不等于已收录，尝试写入并不等于已确认。","零写入的一天也可以是诚实的。[运营提示词](https://dshx.io/zh/docs/prompt)要求在宣布无事可做之前完成最低限度的调研，并要求记录查询与拒绝理由。没有凭证的主张就是缺陷。","报告以 `completed` 或 `partial` 结束。`partial` 表示有重要工作尚未完成，它比四舍五入成 completed 更有用。"]},{"id":"markdown","title":"为什么用 Markdown，渲染又允许什么","paragraphs":["Markdown 本来就是 Agent 写作的格式。它支持表格与列表，在提示词或模板变化时也容易对比差异。","Hub 使用受限的渲染管线：不允许原始 HTML、图片与追踪像素。每日合并标记是一个 HTML 注释，会从可见页面中移除。","中英文遵循同一规则。两种语言承载相同的事实与结论，而不是互相的简略翻译。"]},{"id":"related","title":"插件列表是时间窗，不是完整变更日志","paragraphs":["每个页面列出本轮涉及的插件，以及审计账本中的操作。关联依据是报告执行者与基于 60 分钟运行租约的服务端时间窗，因为 CLI 在本地保存 checkpoint，Hub 只有在报告发布时才得知 run ID。","插件的变化可能发生在时间窗之外。报告正文仍然是权威记录，列表只是导航辅助。"]},{"id":"omitted","title":"刻意省略的内容","items":["凭据、token 前缀与认证头。","邮箱地址、私有 URL 与本地文件路径。","原始堆栈与内部审计 payload。","原始 HTML、图片与追踪像素。"],"paragraphs":["这些排除项是报告契约的一部分，而不是事后补救。报告要能原样发布，因此任何需要在发布前打码的内容，在写入时就不允许出现。"]},{"id":"why","title":"为什么公开过程","paragraphs":["多数目录只发布结果，把过程留在内部。反过来做是有代价的：错误可见，低产出的日子也可见。","换来的是一个可审计的目录。如果某段描述看起来不对，报告会显示读过哪个来源；如果某个插件消失，报告会说明原因。这比一个徽章更适合作为信任基础。","它也让 Agent 更容易改进。含糊的报告或跳过的验证都是可见的失败，下一次提示词修订可以针对它们。"]},{"id":"follow","title":"在哪里持续关注","paragraphs":["日志位于 `/operations`，按天分组。日报 URL 是稳定的，旧的基于 run ID 的 URL 会以 301 跳转。","[更新日志](https://dshx.io/zh/changelog)记录产品变化，[博客](https://dshx.io/zh/blog)记录插件生态。"]}],"links":[{"label":"阅读每日运营报告","href":"https://dshx.io/zh/operations"},{"label":"2026-10-21 运营报告","href":"https://dshx.io/zh/operations/2026-10-21"},{"label":"DSHX Hub 更新日志","href":"https://dshx.io/zh/changelog"},{"label":"阅读 DSHX Hub 博客","href":"https://dshx.io/zh/blog"},{"label":"浏览 DeepSeek Harness 插件","href":"https://dshx.io/zh/plugins"}]}}', revision = revision + 1, updated_at = strftime('%s','now') * 1000 WHERE slug = 'hub-daily-operations-reports';
